  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + weighted) at 0.725 accuracy is the clear best, and all four aggregation×fusion combinations for this exact encoder pair have been tested. No untested configuration uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, and every alternative (resnet50, pca_n2000, scgpt, singleprofile) has been shown to underperform by 1–20+ points. It is highly unlikely any untested config will exceed 0.725. Question: This final experiment provides a cheap RNA-only baseline (scvi_n200, singleprofile, no aggregation) to confirm the magnitude of the multimodal/multiprofile advantage and close the search. Why this is the best use: Since no untested config is expected to beat config_001, the priority shifts to minimizing total GPU hours. config_047 requires only the scvi_n200 RNA encoder on a single profile with no image processing or aggregation, making it the cheapest untested option (estimated ~0.5 GPU hours, well below the 3.6–6.2 hours of multimodal configs). This keeps the total budget near 37.4 GPU hours while still yielding a useful ablation data point."
}

